                <pb facs="0901" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg813"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grip to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Sweden and Norway</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: The consul of Sweden and
                    Norway at Santo Domingo has reported to the Government of the King that the
                    minister of the United States in that capital has had the kindness during the
                    late interior troubles to place a military guard at the disposal of the consul.
                    In regard to this I have received an order from my Government to forward its
                    warmest thanks to the Government of the United States for this act of
                    kindness.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Grip.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
